  <title id="controlloop-title">Block diagram of a closed-loop control system</title>
  <desc id="controlloop-desc">The reference r and the measured output meet at a summing junction that forms the error e. The controller turns e into a command u, the actuator applies it to the plant, and the plant produces the output y. A disturbance d acts on the plant. A sensor, corrupted by noise n, measures y and feeds it back with a negative sign.</desc>
